    "summary": "Epic Dark Star > Other One > Lovelight with tight acoustic interlude",
    "blurb": "The show shines on the monumental Dark Star → The Other One → Lovelight stretch and a beautifully relaxed acoustic segment. Jerry’s lead work is stellar, Phil lays down a strutting bass foundation, and Bob adds strong rhythm and vocal drive. Overall the performance ranks among the strongest late‑1970 shows.",
    "review": "Recorded on February 13, 1970 at the Fillmore East, this three‑set marathon captures the Dead at a creative peak. The first set rolls through classics like China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider and a fiery Smokestack Lightning before settling into an intimate acoustic interlude that later appeared on Bear’s Choice. The second set explodes with a seamless Dark Star → The Other One → Lovelight suite, showcasing Garcia’s soaring tone and improvisational daring, while Phil’s bass locks in tightly and Bob drives the band with his rhythm guitar and vocals. The show closes with Turn On Your Lovelight and a gentle And We Bid You Good Night, leaving listeners with both high‑energy fireworks and heartfelt moments. Across all available recordings the sound is crystal‑clear—especially the Miller soundboard source—making this one of the most listenable and essential 1970 performances.",
